ewright@nc.rr.com (Eric Wright) writes:
> I have a somewhat successful monk going for the first time (I actually
> got to level 14, not that I'm ready to take on Master Kaen yet,
> though), and I have noticed several strange things:
> 
> 1)  The intrinsics gained from increasing levels are not the same you
> gain by eating corpses.  For instance, when I hit level 11, "You feel
> cool".  Not much later, I ate a gelatinous cube corpse and had a
> momentary chill.  What happens if a gremlin attacks and steals my fire
> resistance?  Do I still have it from being at least level 11?  It's
> all very confusing trying to keep track of resistances coming from so
> many sources.

Intrinsically-possessed intrinsics have three sources:

Reaching a certain level (or starting) as a particular role.
Reaching a certain level (or starting) as a particular race.
Other.

Gremlins will remove intrinsics gained from all three of these
sources; level drain from only the first two (and this is the reason
for the difference in messages).

("Intrinsically-possessed", in turn, is just one category of
intrinsics that you can have; others are temporarily-intrinsic,
togglably-intrinsic, and extrinsically-conferred. Yes, this is
confusing, and the term 'intrinsic' doesn't help.)

> 2)  Does it strike anyone else as totally useless that a monk, upon
> crowning, receives a spellbook of restore ability?

Well, it _is_ their specialist spell. But reducing the effectiveness of
unicorn horns is in the other thread.

